# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Slime AI — environment
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Never commit `.env.local`.
# All AI credentials are server-only — they are never sent to the browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Upstream chat provider --------------------------------------------------
# Two interchangeable OpenAI-compatible upstreams — NVIDIA NIM and Groq — set
# ANY ONE (or both) of NVIDIA_API_KEY / GROQ_API_KEY below to chat with real
# models; without either, only the offline mock runs and the internal model
# router is inactive. See src/lib/ai/server/provider.ts.
#
# AI_PROVIDER picks which one is active when both keys are set — "nvidia" or
# "groq". Leave unset to auto-pick: NVIDIA if configured (the
# original/default integration), else Groq. Setting it to a provider whose
# key ISN'T configured falls back to whichever other provider is, rather
# than silently dropping to the offline mock over a one-line env mistake.
# AI_PROVIDER=groq

# NVIDIA NIM free endpoint (https://build.nvidia.com) — OpenAI-compatible.
# Get a free key at build.nvidia.com.
# Default models (all free-endpoint, see src/config/models.ts):
#   nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b · openai/gpt-oss-120b
#   deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro-0813 · nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to the public NVIDIA integrate endpoint.
# NVIDIA_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1

# Optional. JSON array that REPLACES the internal model registry
# (src/config/models.ts). Each entry:
#   { "id", "upstreamId", "contextWindow?", "strengths?", "order?", "image?", "vision?", "endpoint?" }
# `id` is an internal role name (e.g. "slime-reasoning"); `strengths` are task
# categories: general | search | coding | long_context | reasoning | research | structured
# Set "image": true on an entry to enable real image generation in Canvas, and
# set "endpoint" to that model's real NVIDIA invoke URL — NVIDIA hosts most
# image-generation NIMs (Stability, FLUX, etc.) at their own per-model
# function URL, e.g. "https://ai.api.nvidia.com/v1/genai/<org>/<model>", NOT
# the shared chat "/chat/completions" route.
# Set "vision": true on an entry (default registry ships one:
# meta/llama-3.2-11b-vision-instruct) to let it answer questions about an
# attached image — it speaks the shared chat/completions route, just with
# OpenAI-style image_url content, so no "endpoint" override is needed.
# NVIDIA_MODELS=[{"id":"slime-general","upstreamId":"meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct","contextWindow":128000,"strengths":["general"],"order":1}]
#
# As of the last audit (nvidia_free_model_ids.txt, 39 free-endpoint models),
# NVIDIA's free tier has NO genuine text-to-image model — only chat/reasoning,
# image-understanding (vision-in/text-out), speech/TTS, embeddings, safety,
# and video/perception nets. Image Gen mode is fully wired end-to-end and
# will light up the moment a real image-capable free-endpoint model ships;
# until then it reports the capability gap instead of faking a result. Image
# *understanding* (a real vision model) IS wired in the default registry.

# Groq (https://console.groq.com) — OpenAI-compatible, known for very fast
# inference. Default models (src/config/models.ts) are best-effort — built
# from long-standing Groq-hosted model families, but NOT verified against a
# live `GET /v1/models` call (no network access to Groq's API from where
# these defaults were written). Check your own key's model list and override
# anything stale with GROQ_MODELS below before relying on this in production;
# a wrong id just fails loudly and the router moves to the next entry, it
# doesn't fail silently.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to Groq's OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1

# Optional. Same shape/rules as NVIDIA_MODELS above — JSON array that
# REPLACES the Groq model registry. No "image" support (Groq doesn't offer
# image generation); Image Gen mode stays NVIDIA-specific regardless of
# AI_PROVIDER. No default "vision": true entry ships either (see the comment
# on DEFAULT_GROQ_MODELS in src/config/models.ts for why) — add one here,
# once you've confirmed a current vision-capable model id, to let image
# attachments work while Groq is the active provider.
# GROQ_MODELS=[{"id":"slime-general","upstreamId":"llama-3.3-70b-versatile","contextWindow":128000,"strengths":["general"],"order":1}]

# Optional. Upstream request timeout in ms (default 60000).
# AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# Optional. Max router attempts per request: primary + fallbacks (default 3, range 1–6).
# AI_MAX_FALLBACKS=3

# Optional. Enables real web search grounding for Search mode (Firecrawl's
# /v1/search API — https://firecrawl.dev). Without it, Search mode still
# routes to the fast model as before, it just answers from the model's own
# knowledge and says so plainly rather than faking results.
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
